    "updated_at": "2017-02-20T16:08:33Z",
    "body": "Yes, there is generally some implicit conversion between IDL types and their corresponding ES type. Would you prefer if I explicitly inserted \"the corresponding IDL object\" or \"the corresponding ES object\" conversion steps? It seems like unnecessary boilerplate to me. Maybe I could add a sentence to the definition of the construction stack, or to the intro of the custom element section, stating that we do such implicit coercions? Or perhaps to the intro of the HTML spec itself?",
